{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1215839-exigent-idea-chosen-of-parody-and-satire","id":1215839,"title":"Exigent Idea: Chosen of Parody and Satire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-06T10:11:26-07:00","id":1215839,"title":"Exigent Idea: Chosen of Parody and Satire","content":"I am jumping the gun by a long shot, but the idea won't leave my brain.<br /> <br /> After binging on postmodernist humor for a bit, I remembered something I heard from Wisecrack, that parody and satire are two sides of literary criticism in literature; both mock the underpinnings of a work or genre, but satire is made with the intent of destroying its subject, while parody seeks to improve it. Where <i>Watchmen</i> wants to show how ineffective and dangerous superheroes are, <i>One Punch Man</i> is showing how hilariously meaningless it is to make an OP character that warps the plot while showing that superheroes can still work without a Superman. (Their example, not mine.)<br /> <br /> While I don't claim to be anywhere near an expert, I will say that's a good Yin-Yang dichotomy. One destroys, the other creates, but through the same method. So, let's make it mystical! <br /> <br /> Idea is that the God of a library invoked the Exigence to empower a scribe with the power to criticize the Fair Folk to death by attacking their narrative underpinnings. However, criticism is such a vast field of philosophy that the new Exaltation underwent mitosis, creating a new Exigence that had the capacity to improve Creation by bringing its flaws to the fore and diagnosing solutions. Both have similar powers, but one is meant to assault and deconstruct through narrative, the other support and improve. Both of them also belong to introspective, didactitc smartasses with an axe to grind, because seriously, it's still Satire and Parody.<br /> <br /> So I was wondering, what kind of power do you think these two have that enforce the theme of Narrative and Critique?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T11:23:23-07:00","id":1215863,"title":"","content":"His name is Red-Daubed Pool of the Dead, and all the Deathlords are very confused because that makes them think he's one of theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5771-krata-lightblade","name":"Krata Lightblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T12:25:04-07:00","id":1215871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krata Lightblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/1215839-exigent-idea-chosen-of-parody-and-satire?p=1215863#post1215863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His name is Red-D